# Team 26 — Analysis Plan

## Overview

Outcome: share of SSH abstracts framed in collectivist vs. individualist terms (LLM-classified).
IV: `v2x_libdem` (continuous, 0-1). Unit: country-year. Estimator: `fixest::feols` with country + year FE, SE clustered by `iso3`.

---

## Step 0 — Load corpus

File: `analysis/00_load.R`

Load `data/agent_corpus.rds`. Confirm columns: `wos_id` (or `ut`), `abstract`, `iso3`, `year`, `v2x_libdem`, `v2x_regime`, `lied_binary`, `e_gdppc`, `e_wb_pop`, `subject_primary`.

---

## Step 1 — Draw stratified sample

File: `analysis/01_sample.R`

`set.seed(42)`. Keep abstracts with `nchar(abstract) > 50`. Add `decade = (year %/% 10) * 10`. Use `group_by(iso3, v2x_regime, decade) |> slice_sample(n = 10)`. Target ~7,000-8,000 rows.

Save: `data/team26_sample.rds`, `data/team26_sample.csv`.

---

## Step 2 — LLM classification

File: `analysis/02_classify.R`

Model: Claude Haiku 3 (primary); GPT-4o-mini (fallback). Hard stop if running cost > $20.

Prompt: single-turn per abstract, returns exactly one label: `COLLECTIVIST`, `INDIVIDUALIST`, or `MIXED-NEUTRAL`. Full prompt text in `rq.md`.

Notes:
- Batch calls with rate-limiting delay.
- Accumulate token cost estimate (~$0.00025/1K for Haiku); log to `output/team26_api_cost_log.txt`.
- Write incrementally to `data/team26_classifications_raw.csv` (columns: `wos_id`, `label`, `model`, `tokens_used`). Skip already-classified IDs on resume.

Validation: manually label 50 of a 100-abstract holdout; compute Cohen's kappa against LLM labels; save to `output/team26_validation.txt`. If kappa < 0.60, revise prompt before full run.

---

## Step 3 — Aggregate to country-year

File: `analysis/03_aggregate.R`

Join classifications to corpus on `wos_id`. For each `iso3` x `year` cell compute:
- `n_classified`, `n_collectivist`, `n_individualist`, `n_mixed`
- `share_collectivist = n_collectivist / (n_collectivist + n_individualist)` (MIXED-NEUTRAL excluded from denominator)
- `share_individualist = n_individualist / (n_collectivist + n_individualist)`

Filter to cells with `n_classified >= 5`. Carry through regime and control variables from first row.

Save: `data/team26_country_year.rds`.

---

## Step 4 — Primary models

File: `analysis/04_models.R`

```r
library(fixest)
df <- readRDS("data/team26_country_year.rds") |>
  mutate(log_gdppc = log(e_gdppc), log_pop = log(e_wb_pop))

# Primary: share_collectivist
m1 <- feols(share_collectivist ~ v2x_libdem | iso3 + year, data = df, cluster = ~iso3)
m2 <- feols(share_collectivist ~ v2x_libdem + log_gdppc + log_pop | iso3 + year, data = df, cluster = ~iso3)

# Secondary: share_individualist
m3 <- feols(share_individualist ~ v2x_libdem | iso3 + year, data = df, cluster = ~iso3)
m4 <- feols(share_individualist ~ v2x_libdem + log_gdppc + log_pop | iso3 + year, data = df, cluster = ~iso3)
```

Expected direction: `v2x_libdem` negative for `share_collectivist` (more autocracy = more collectivist framing); positive for `share_individualist`.

